=== {{S|étymologie}} ===
: {{term|bras}} Du {{étyl|ang|en|mot=earm}}{{R|etymonline}} apparenté à {{lien|''Arm''|de|sens=}} en allemand, {{lien|''armus''|la|sens=épaule}} en latin.
: {{term|arme, armer}} {{siècle|lang=en|XIV}} De l’{{étyl|fro|fro|mot=arme}}, {{lien|''armer''|fr}}.

=== {{S|nom|en|num=1}} ===
{{en-nom-rég|ɑːm|pron2=ɑɹm}}
[[Image:Arm.agr.jpg|thumb|A human '''arm''']]
'''arm''' {{pron|ɑːm|en}} {{UK|nocat=1}} <small>ou</small> {{pron|ɑɹm|en}} {{USA|nocat=1}}
# {{lexique|anatomie|en}} [[bras#fr|Bras]].
#*{{exemple|She stood with her right '''arm''' extended and her palm forward to indicate “Stop!”|lang=en}}
# [[manche#fr|Manche]].
#*{{exemple|…one '''arm''' of this jacket streamed behind him like the broidered arm of a huzzar’s surcoat.|source={{w|Herman Melville}}, ''Moby-Dick'', 1851|lang=en}}
# {{figuré|en}} Bras, pouvoir.
#*{{exemple|The secular '''arm'''.|Le bras séculier.|lang=en}}
# [[accoudoir#fr|Accoudoir]].
#*{{exemple|lang=en}}

==== {{S|dérivés}} ====
* {{lien|armchair|en|sens=fauteuil}}
* {{lien|arm in arm|en|sens=bras dessus, bras dessous}}
* {{lien|armless|en|sens=}}
* {{lien|armrest|en|sens=accoudoir}}
* {{lien|forearm|en|sens=avant-bras}}

=== {{S|nom|en|num=2}} ===
{{en-nom-rég|ɑːm|pron2=ɑɹm}}
'''arm''' {{pron|ɑːm|en}} {{usage}} rare au singulier.
# {{armes|en}} [[arme#fr|Arme]].
#*{{exemple|A well regulated Militia, being necessary to the security of a free state, the right of the people to keep and bear '''arms''', shall not be infringed.|source=''{{ws|United States Bill of Rights|lang=en}}'', 1789|lang=en}}
# {{au pluriel}} {{lexique|héraldique|en}} [[armoiries#fr|Armoiries]].
#*{{exemple|The Duke's '''arms''' were a sable gryphon rampant on an argent field.|lang=en}}

==== {{S|synonymes}} ====
* {{lien|weapon|en}}

==== {{S|dérivés}} ====
* {{lien|coat of arms|en|sens=armoiries}}
* {{lien|firearm|en|sens=arme à feu}}

=== {{S|verbe|en}} ===
{{en-conj-rég|inf.pron=ɑːm}}
'''arm''' {{pron|ɑːm|en}}
# [[armer#fr|Armer]].
#* {{exemple|lang=en}}

